# Lobsy design system (calm UI)

**Docs:** [`README.md`](../../README.md) · [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) · [`docs/ONBOARDING.md`](../../docs/ONBOARDING.md) · [`CONTRIBUTING.md`](../../CONTRIBUTING.md) · [`docs/ROUTES.md`](../../docs/ROUTES.md) · [`docs/adr/`](../../docs/adr/) · [`docs/security/roles-matrix.md`](../../docs/security/roles-matrix.md) · [`Jobsy.Tests/README.md`](../../Jobsy.Tests/README.md).

Mobile-first, calm UI for candidate and employer surfaces. Prefer clarity over decoration.

## Principles

- **One primary action per screen** — one clear CTA; secondary actions stay quiet (text link or outline).
- **Calm surfaces** — pearl / soft neutrals (`--bg`, `--surface`, `--pearl-*`); navy brand (`--brand`, `--accent`).
- **Status is never color-only** — always pair color with a label and/or icon.
- **Dutch UI copy** on candidate-facing screens unless the active language is overridden.
- **Mobile first** — two-column grids collapse cleanly; bottom nav clearance via `--bottom-nav-clearance`.

## Tokens

Defined in `Jobsy.Web/wwwroot/css/app.css` `:root`:

- Brand / accent: `--brand`, `--accent`, `--accent-soft`, `--accent-deep`
- Feedback: `--success` / `--success-soft`, `--warn`, `--danger`
- Neutrals: `--bg`, `--surface`, `--text`, `--muted`, `--border`
- **Gold (paid / extended):** `--gold` (#c9a227), `--gold-light`, `--gold-deep`, `--gold-ink`, `--gold-soft`, `--gold-gradient`

## Gold exception

Gradients are otherwise avoided for chrome and tiles. **Exception:** a subtle gold gradient (`--gold-gradient`) is allowed **only** for:

1. Gold primary buttons (extended / paid upsell CTAs)
2. Gold accent bars on test tiles when the extended version is completed

Do not use gold gradients for backgrounds, heroes, or decorative fills.

## Test status colors

| Status | Token | Label (NL) |
|--------|--------|------------|
| Free completed | `--success` | Gratis gedaan |
| Extended / paid completed | `--gold` | Uitgebreid |
| Not taken | gray / muted | Nog niet gedaan |

If both free and extended are done, **gold wins**.

## Public theme (landing, gratis test, public info pages)

Approved deviations valid **only inside `.pub-theme`** (`wwwroot/css/features/public-theme.css`, root class on `PublicLayout`):

1. Warm tints mixed from existing tokens with `color-mix()` (`--gold`, `--coral`, `--success`, `--brand` with `--surface`); coral may appear several times per screen; navy only for the primary CTA and text. No new hex values.
2. Radii 24/36 px for cards and scenes, pill-shaped buttons.
3. Public type sizes: hero h1 `3.25rem` desktop / `2.125rem` mobile, h2 `2.25rem`, result h1 `3rem`, and 700 weight on h2s. Defined once as `--pub-text-*` custom properties.
4. Emoji as icons (next to some headings, in chips and buttons), always `aria-hidden` with a text label next to them.
5. Organic blobs, waves and illustration scenes (inline SVG or CSS), plus one extra soft shadow `--pub-shadow-soft` (coral-tinted), public theme only.
6. Likert buttons with emoji faces; blur on the locked passport teaser.

Still binding inside `.pub-theme`: tokens only, no inline `style=""` in `.razor` (use CSS custom properties set via classes, or `style` only for a computed `--pct` value as existing components do), breakpoints 640/900/1024 only, logical properties, tap targets ≥ 44 px, focus rings visible, contrast AA (the -zw and ON palettes both pass; a test checks the main text/background pairs), `prefers-reduced-motion` fallbacks, and **no `!important`** (the mockup CSS uses a few; the implementation must not).

**The logged-in app is untouched**: no `pub-` class and no `public-theme.css` rule may affect a page under `MainLayout`.

BEM blocks (shell in file 01; later files add `pub-landing__…`, `pub-test__…`, `pub-signup__…`): `pub-header`, `pub-nav`, `pub-menu`, `pub-footer`, `pub-lang`, `pub-btn` (`--primary` / `--secondary` / `--ghost`), `pub-chip`, `pub-card`, `pub-eyebrow`, `pub-section` (`--alt`, `--wave-top` / `--wave-bottom`), `pub-emoji`, `pub-pill-sample`.
